From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: omarchy-asus <noreply@github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] EXPERIMENTAL: PM: sleep: log the SMU idlemask after each PCI
 device's noirq suspend (pm_debug_messages only)

EXPERIMENTAL, DEBUG ONLY (local carry for ROG Zephyrus G16 GA605KM idle
power testing; not submitted upstream).

On the G16, 9904's trace shows idlemask bits 16-19 turning idle between
"s2idle-prepare" and "amdgpu-noirq", and bits 5, 20 and 25 by "noirq",
while amdgpu's own noirq callback does nothing in s2idle there. So the
noirq phase of other devices idles them: the PCI core puts each device
into D3 in pci_pm_suspend_noirq(). Log the idlemask once as the noirq
phase starts and after each PCI device's noirq suspend:

  SMU idlemask noirq-start: 0x...
  SMU idlemask noirq <device> <power state>: 0x...

for example "SMU idlemask noirq 0000:65:00.0 D3hot: 0x...". The power
state is the one the noirq suspend left the device in (pci_power_name()).
A device suspended asynchronously logs from its async thread when it
finishes, so the lines are in the order the devices finished. Devices
skipped by direct_complete or syscore don't log; non-PCI devices don't
either, to keep the log readable.

It goes through 9904's amd_pmc_trace_idlemask_stage() (symbol_get() of
amd_pmc's exported trace), so the PM core does not depend on amd_pmc.
Only in an s2idle (PM_EVENT_SUSPEND to PM_SUSPEND_TO_IDLE).

Nothing is read or logged unless /sys/power/pm_debug_messages is 1 during
an s2idle. With it at 0 nothing changes.

Tracked in omarchy-asus #353 (refs #249).
---
diff --git a/drivers/base/power/main.c b/drivers/base/power/main.c
--- a/drivers/base/power/main.c
+++ b/drivers/base/power/main.c
@@ -37,6 +37,8 @@
 #include <linux/thermal.h>
 #include <linux/timer.h>
 #include <linux/nmi.h>
+#include <linux/pci.h>
+#include <linux/platform_data/x86/amd-pmc.h>
 
 #include "../base.h"
 #include "power.h"
@@ -1494,6 +1496,37 @@
 
 static void async_suspend_noirq(void *data, async_cookie_t cookie);
 
+/*
+ * EXPERIMENTAL: in an s2idle with pm_debug_messages on, log the SMU idlemask
+ * (through amd_pmc) as the noirq phase starts and after each PCI device's
+ * noirq suspend, with the power state that left the device in. A no-op
+ * otherwise, and without amd_pmc loaded.
+ */
+static bool dpm_noirq_trace_idlemask_on(pm_message_t state)
+{
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_AMD_PMC) && defined(CONFIG_PM_SLEEP_DEBUG)
+	return state.event == PM_EVENT_SUSPEND &&
+	       pm_suspend_target_state == PM_SUSPEND_TO_IDLE &&
+	       pm_debug_messages_should_print();
+#else
+	return false;
+#endif
+}
+
+static void dpm_noirq_trace_idlemask(struct device *dev, pm_message_t state)
+{
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_AMD_PMC) && defined(CONFIG_PM_SLEEP_DEBUG) && defined(CONFIG_PCI)
+	char stage[64];
+
+	if (!dev_is_pci(dev) || !dpm_noirq_trace_idlemask_on(state))
+		return;
+
+	snprintf(stage, sizeof(stage), "noirq %s %s", dev_name(dev),
+		 pci_power_name(to_pci_dev(dev)->current_state));
+	amd_pmc_trace_idlemask_stage(stage);
+#endif
+}
+
 /**
  * device_suspend_noirq - Execute a "noirq suspend" callback for given device.
  * @dev: Device to handle.
@@ -1555,6 +1588,7 @@
 
 Skip:
 	dev->power.is_noirq_suspended = true;
+	dpm_noirq_trace_idlemask(dev, state);
 
 	/*
 	 * Devices must be resumed unless they are explicitly allowed to be left
@@ -1595,6 +1629,9 @@
 
 	trace_suspend_resume(TPS("dpm_suspend_noirq"), state.event, true);
 
+	if (dpm_noirq_trace_idlemask_on(state))
+		amd_pmc_trace_idlemask_stage("noirq-start");
+
 	pm_transition = state;
 	async_error = 0;
 
